# Module: Dropdown

## Dropdown-UC1 — Get Current Selection ID

- Primary Actor(s): User
- Secondary Actor(s): System
- Trigger: User selects an item from the dropdown list.
- Description: This use case retrieves the currently selected value from a dropdown list and returns its ID if it's valid.
- Preconditions: A dropdown list exists with selectable items.
- Postconditions: The ID of the selected item is retrieved or returns 0 if no valid selection is made.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. User selects an item from the dropdown list.
  2. System checks if the selected value is not null or empty.
  3. System attempts to parse the selected value into an integer.
  4. System returns the integer value if successful; otherwise returns 0.
- Extensions: None
- Exceptions: None
- Business Rules: If the ID cannot be parsed, 0 is returned.
- Assumptions: Dropdown list contains items with non-empty values.
- Open Issues: None

## Dropdown-UC2 — Reset Dropdown Selection

- Primary Actor(s): User
- Secondary Actor(s): System
- Trigger: User action to clear the selection.
- Description: This use case resets the selection of a dropdown list, clearing any selected item.
- Preconditions: A dropdown list exists and has items.
- Postconditions: The dropdown list selection is cleared.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. User requests to reset the dropdown selection.
  2. System checks if the dropdown list is not null.
  3. System clears the current selection in the dropdown list.
- Extensions: None
- Exceptions: If the dropdown list is null, the operation is aborted.
- Business Rules: None
- Assumptions: The dropdown list is typically non-null.
- Open Issues: None

## Dropdown-UC3 — Select Value in Dropdown

- Primary Actor(s): User
- Secondary Actor(s): System
- Trigger: User specifies a value to be selected in the dropdown list.
- Description: This use case allows the user to specify a value to be selected within a dropdown list.
- Preconditions: The dropdown list contains items.
- Postconditions: The specified value is selected if it exists in the dropdown.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. User provides a value for selection.
  2. System iterates over each item in the dropdown list.
  3. System finds an item matching the specified value.
  4. System clears previous selections and selects the item.
  5. System confirms the selection was successful.
- Extensions: If no matching value is found, the operation fails silently.
- Exceptions: None
- Business Rules: Only one item can be selected at a time.
- Assumptions: The dropdown list values are unique.
- Open Issues: None

## Dropdown-UC4 — Select Text in Dropdown

- Primary Actor(s): User
- Secondary Actor(s): System
- Trigger: User specifies text to be selected in the dropdown list.
- Description: This use case allows the user to specify text to be selected within a dropdown list.
- Preconditions: The dropdown list contains items.
- Postconditions: The specified text is selected if it exists in the dropdown.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. User provides text for selection.
  2. System iterates over each item in the dropdown list.
  3. System finds an item matching the specified text.
  4. System clears previous selections and selects the item.
  5. System confirms the selection was successful.
- Extensions: If no matching text is found, the operation fails silently.
- Exceptions: None
- Business Rules: Only one item can be selected at a time.
- Assumptions: The dropdown list texts are unique.
- Open Issues: None

## Dropdown-UC5 — Get Value from Text

- Primary Actor(s): User
- Secondary Actor(s): System
- Trigger: User wants to find the value corresponding to specific text in the dropdown list.
- Description: This use case retrieves the value of an item in the dropdown list based on its text.
- Preconditions: The dropdown list contains items.
- Postconditions: The value associated with the specified text is retrieved.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. User provides text whose value they wish to find.
  2. System iterates over each item in the dropdown list.
  3. System finds an item with the specified text.
  4. System retrieves the value of the matched item.
  5. System returns the value to the user.
- Extensions: If no matching text is found, an empty value is returned.
- Exceptions: None
- Business Rules: Text and values are stored as key-value pairs.
- Assumptions: Texts are unique for each value in the dropdown list.
- Open Issues: None

## Dropdown-UC6 — Add Missing Item

- Primary Actor(s): User
- Secondary Actor(s): System
- Trigger: User needs to add an item that is currently not in the active list but is the selected value.
- Description: This use case allows adding an item to the dropdown when it is not active but needs to be selected.
- Preconditions: The dropdown list is editable.
- Postconditions: The new item is added to the dropdown list.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. User specifies the name and ID for the new item.
  2. System creates a new list item with the specified name and ID.
  3. System inserts the new item at the top of the dropdown list.
- Extensions: None
- Exceptions: None
- Business Rules: The new item can be inserted without affecting the existing selection if it is the selected item.
- Assumptions: Dropdown items are typically added at the start position.
- Open Issues: None

## Dropdown-UC7 — Remove All Except Selected Item

- Primary Actor(s): User
- Secondary Actor(s): System
- Trigger: User wishes to keep only the currently selected item in the dropdown list.
- Description: This use case removes all items from the dropdown list except the currently selected one.
- Preconditions: At least one item is selected in the dropdown list.
- Postconditions: Only the selected item remains in the dropdown list.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. User requests to keep only the selected item.
  2. System retrieves the currently selected item.
  3. System clears all items from the dropdown list.
  4. System adds the saved item back to the dropdown list.
  5. System sets the saved item as the selected item.
- Extensions: None
- Exceptions: None
- Business Rules: Ensures the dropdown list is not empty after the operation.
- Assumptions: At least one item is always selected before this operation.
- Open Issues: None